./CLAUDE.md:65:**Holistic sweep:** fully crosses the flight-time drivers — airframe × battery × SBC × VTX × thermal camera — holds the sub-1 W peripherals (FPV cam, GPS, RX) at lightest representatives, then **filters out incompatible pairings** per the model's `Compatibility` rules: **P1** battery↔airframe cell-count (drops e.g. a 4S pack on a 6S-only frame) and **V2** thermal↔DVR (a thermal no DVR can record — raw SPI/CMOS — is dropped). The **DVR is not crossed and is excluded from flight time**: it is an earlier-stage (Phase 1-2) part, so the headline endurance is the SBC-stage build (SBC present, DVR removed); the DVR is kept only for earlier-stage camera↔DVR compatibility and for cost. **Thermal camera locked to T13** (PurpleRiver Mini 640) via `FIXED_THERMAL_ID` and **SBC locked to SBC3** (NanoPi M5, RK3576) via `FIXED_SBC_ID` — David's design choices, so neither is swept (set either to `None` to sweep all again). With T13 + SBC3 fixed: **186 real configs** (all meet R4). Falls back to a generated generic LiPo/Li-ion grid only if no Battery candidates exist in `candidates.sysml`. **15 of 16 airframes participate** (AF5/EMAX Hawk 7 still lacks a confirmed mass; the discontinued KOLAS7 PNP and GEPRC MARK4 LR7 were removed 2026-06-27 — MARK4 replaced by the GEPRC MOZ7 V2 family: AF1a Analog / AF1b WTFPV / AF1c O4 Pro). **Recommended baseline:** DarwinFPV 129 (AF9a) + 4S 12Ah Amprius + T13 + SBC3 → 69.1 min hover, ~$1,505 system (well under the $2,500 R4 cap). (The earlier KOLAS7 "71 min winner" was a data artifact — its modeled mass omitted the 188 g of motors; corrected to as-built ~540–565 g, see `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §D.) See also `MODEL_ISSUES.md` §C11-C12.
